# 📋 Framework: Handling Completed Failed Jobs

## I. Definition & Scope
A **completed failed job** = execution terminated, status = failed, no longer running — distinct from stuck/pending jobs.

| Category | Description |
|---|---|
| Transient failure | Network blip, rate limit, temporary unavailability — likely to succeed on retry |
| Permanent failure | Bad input, invalid config, missing resource, auth error — will fail again unless fixed |
| Systemic failure | Shared outage, schema change, downstream API shift — affects multiple jobs |

---

## II. Capture & Preservation — Don't Lose Context
Before anything else: **freeze the evidence** so you can understand *why* it failed.

### What to Preserve
- Full payload/input parameters
- Timestamps: started, ended, duration
- Error stack trace, exit code, logs
- Attempt number, max retries
- Worker/node/environment info
- Partial outputs, checkpoints, side-effects state

### DLQ Pattern (Dead-Letter Queue) — Standard Industry Approach
```
┌─────────────┐     retry × N      ┌─────────────┐
│  Retry Loop │ ────────────────→ │  DLQ / Dead │
│ (active/failed)                 │  Jobs Store │
└─────────────┘                   └─────┬───────┘
                                        │
                     inspect → diagnose → fix → replay or archive
```
- **Never auto-delete** after final failure — move to DLQ instead
- **Never auto-replay** entire DLQ — fixes get re-broken; only replay after root-cause resolution
- **Alert on DLQ growth** — rising count = systemic issue
- **Set retention/TTL** — archive after configurable period (e.g., 30–90 days)

### Schema Example
```sql
CREATE TABLE dead_letter_jobs (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY,
  original_type TEXT NOT NULL,
  payload JSONB,
  error_summary TEXT,
  error_stack TEXT,
  attempt_count INT DEFAULT 1,
  max_attempts INT,
  first_failed_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
  last_failed_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
  status TEXT DEFAULT 'pending_review', -- pending_review, fixed, replayed, archived
  replay_job_id UUID,
  notes TEXT -- for RCA findings
);
```

