## III. Diagnosis Workflow — Step-by-Step

### 1. Triage & Classify
| Check | Action |
|---|---|
| Same error across many jobs? | → Systemic issue — stop individual replays, fix the root cause first |
| Intermittent / time-related? | → Transient — safe to retry with backoff+jitter |
| Consistent same failure? | → Permanent — fix data/code/config first |
| Dependent on already-run succeeded work? | → Idempotency check needed — avoid duplicates |

### 2. Check Idempotency Before Replay
- **Replay from start** = may duplicate already-completed work → use only when downstream state is corrupted
- **Resume from failure point** = use checkpoints/partial progress tracking — safer, preserves outputs
- **Mark as succeeded** (manual override) = when failure is known-harmless or externally resolved — clears from backlog without re-running

### 3. RCA (Root Cause Analysis) — 5-Why for Jobs
1. What exactly failed? (error message + stack)
2. What input/state triggered it?
3. What changed since last success? (code, config, data, upstream API)
4. What should have happened instead?
5. What prevents this from being caught earlier?

